    eEn: "Memory modules with 'Made in India' on them, shipped to Dell and HP, are a real first and worth recording plainly.\n\nThey are also the easier half of the job. Packaging and testing chips needs capital and skill, but the high-value step, fabricating the silicon, is still not done at commercial scale in India, and the sources disagree about when the first fab will be ready.\n\nIt is fair to be pleased by the first milestone and honest about the second. The right test is not the next inauguration but whether a fab produces chips someone pays for.",
