    eEn: "In February, the announced tariff on Indian goods going to the United States fell from 50% to 18%. That was real relief for exporters, and it deserves to be recorded as such.\n\nBut nine months later we could not find a signed agreement, and one report says the legal basis for those tariffs has been contested in the US courts. For a business that prices a shipment months ahead, a rate that might change is almost as costly as a high one.\n\nThe lesson is not about either government's skill. It is that a framework announced at a summit is the start of a process, and the numbers that count are the ones in a signed text.",
